course: dictionary
lesson: 7042
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: The word pass has more than one meaning, so you must read the words around it to know which one fits. «Time passes slowly in a long lesson» means time goes by. «We passed the school on the way home» means we went past it.
explain: Try the meaning in the sentence to check it. «Please pass the ball to Maya» means give the ball to her, not go past it. If your meaning makes the sentence silly, choose another meaning and try again.
explain: Pass can also be a noun, a thing. In sport, a pass is a kick or throw of the ball to a teammate. «Her pass to the winger led to a goal» means her kick or throw to the winger.
fact: To pass something means to give it to the next person.
fact: To pass means to go by or go past something, like «We passed the school».
fact: To pass a test means to do well enough in it.
fact: Time passes when it goes by, as in «The days pass quickly».
fact: A pass is a kick or throw of the ball to a teammate, or a ticket that lets you in.
exercise: «Please pass the ball to Maya.» What does pass mean here? | To lose it in the grass | To go past the ball without touching it | To fail the game | *To give it to the next person
exercise: «We passed the school on the way home.» What does passed mean? | Did well enough in a test | *Went by or went past | Gave the school to someone | Stopped to play in the playground
exercise: In «Her pass to the winger was perfect», what kind of word is pass? | A question word | *A noun, a kick or throw to a teammate | An adjective, describing the winger | A verb, meaning to sleep
test: «She must pass the test to move up a class.» What does pass mean? | To give the test to someone else | *To do well enough in it | To go past the test without looking | To lose the test paper
test: «Time passes when we are having fun.» What does passes mean? | Is given to a friend | *Goes by | Gets bigger and bigger | Stops completely
exam: «When passing a horse and rider, slow down, give lots of room and say hello.» What should you do when you pass a horse? | Stand right in front of the horse | *Slow down, give lots of room and say hello | Shout and run past quickly | Pass the rider a ball to play with
